  "comment": "Regression gate limits (tools/check_bench.py --baseline), Task 5c fix round 2. Release builds align code (ZODIAC_RELEASE_CODE_ALIGN=blocks) and the bench carries the shipped manifest (the Segment Heap). Each of a side's 3 processes runs from its own copy of its build on one Windows runner; a process's time is Zodiac's ns over its machine-speed factor, the add-on side's median over operations against the processes of its own side only. Per operation the gate compares head's best process with main's median process; the geometric mean compares best with best. Data: 40 gate-replica A/A' jobs in which head and main were linked with different no-op relink pads (ZODIAC_BENCH_PAD and ZODIAC_BENCH_CORE_PAD; every job a different pair, all 8 pairs 5 times), so the samples hold the layout shift a change elsewhere in the code causes as well as process and placement noise: 45590935252, 45590944030, 45590950054, 45590955784, 45590961395 (54a811c); EPYC 7763 18, EPYC 9V74 11, EPYC 9V45 8, Xeon 8573C 3. An A/A' job is symmetric in its labels, so each gives two samples of the per-operation statistic (head best over main median, and main best over head median): 80 per operation. Rule, for x = ln(statistic): limit = exp(median(x) + 3.540 * 1.4826 * MAD(x) * b), b = sqrt(n / chi-square 5 % quantile with n degrees of freedom), rounded up to 0.01; never below the largest sample plus 1 % rounded up, and never below 1.03 (\"floor\": true where one of those two decides). The geometric mean's limit: exp(3.291 * s_upper), s the root mean square of its ln about 0 (samples 0.988-1.019, RMS 0.59 %). The model figure (0.02 % per operation, 0.05 % for the geometric mean) is not a measurement; what the data supports is the held-out count: limits from 39 jobs failed none of the 40 held out one at a time, 0 false failures in 40 gate runs, and the validation replicas run with this file are recorded in spec 8.4 and the Task 5c report (fix round 2). An operation not listed takes the default 1.10 until gate-replica samples set its own.",
